  "term": "mercy",
  "definition": "Mercy is a character trait that leads a person to lessen penalties that could justly be imposed for wrongdoing. In the source, it is contrasted with justice because it softens what is deserved, and distinguished from compassion because compassion responds mainly to suffering rather than to blameworthiness.",
